## 1. What was failing and why

The test `base-terminator-allows-dash-pattern` invokes `rust_grep -- -alpha a.txt`. The `--` should end option parsing and make `-alpha` the pattern. However, in the argument-parsing loop, the "unsupported option" check (`b[0] == b'-' && b.len() > 1`) fires **before** the `b == b"--"` check. Since `--` itself starts with `-` and has length > 1, the program calls `usage_exit()` on the `--` token itself, never reaching the code that sets `after_ddash = true`.

## 2. What I changed

